The dataset contains data for dihydroxylammonium 5,5’-bistetrazole-1,1’-diolate (TKX-50), ammonium perchlorate (AP), and TKX-50/AP cocrystal across a temperature range of 300–4000 K. The initial structures consist of a 2 × 1 × 2 supercell of TKX-50, a 1 × 2 × 1 supercell of AP, and a 2 × 1 × 1 supercell of the TKX-50/AP cocrystal. The dataset is divided into two parts: the first part comprises the initial data generated by AIMD , with filenames labeled as "init"; the second part includes data produced through the active learning strategy of the dpgen program, with filenames labeled as "dpgen."A hybrid Gaussian plane wave scheme based on the DZVP–MOLOPT–SR–GTH basis set was employed . The exchange-correlation interaction between itinerant electrons was treated using the Perdew–Burke–Ernzerhof functional, for which a plane-wave cutoff energy of 400 Ry was used . The Grimme DFT-D3 method was used to account for dispersion interactions.
Please cite the reference: https://doi.org/https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2026.138315